secure remote connections\n- **Deployment Modifications**: Inject sidecars, volumes, environment variables\n- **Resource Templates**: Generate Traefik IngressRoutes, Middlewares, NetworkPolicies\n\n### **Key Components**\n\n#### **Controllers** (`internal/controller/`)\n- **WorkspaceController**: Reconciles workspace state, manages deployments/services/PVCs\n- **WorkspaceTemplateController**: Manages template lifecycle and finalizers\n- **WorkspaceAccessStrategyController**: Processes access strategy templates\n- **State Machine**: Handles workspace lifecycle (Pending → Running → Stopped → Degraded)\n- **Idle Checker**: Monitors workspace activity via HTTP probes, triggers auto-shutdown\n\n#### **Extension API Server** (`internal/extensionapi/`)\nCustom API server providing:\n- **Connection Management**: Generate connection URLs/tokens for workspaces\n- **Authorization**: Kubernetes SubjectAccessReview integration\n- **JWT Signing**: AWS KMS-backed token generation for secure connections\n- **WebSocket Support**: Real-time connection handling (planned)\n- **Discovery Endpoint**: List available workspaces for users\n\n#### **Auth Middleware** (`internal/authmiddleware/`)\nTraefik ForwardAuth middleware providing:\n- **OIDC Authentication**: Dex integration for GitHub/LDAP/SAML\n- **Bearer Token Auth**: JWT validation for programmatic access\n- **Cookie Management**: Session handling with secure cookies\n- **Workspace Authorization**: Verifies user permissions via Kubernetes RBAC\n\n#### **Webhooks** (`internal/webhook/v1alpha1/`)\nAdmission webhooks for validation:\n- **Workspace Validation**: Template compliance, resource bounds, ownership checks\n- **Template Immutability**: Prevents spec changes after creation\n- **Pod Exec Security**: Restricts `kubectl exec` to workspace owners only\n\n### **Deployment Modes**\n\n#### **Guided Mode** (Full Stack)\nHelm chart deploys complete infrastructure:\n- **Traefik**: Reverse proxy with dynamic routing\n- **Dex**: OIDC identity provider (GitHub OAuth)\n- **Cert-Manager**: Automatic TLS certificates (Let's Encrypt)\n- **Auth Middleware**: Authentication/authorization layer\n- **Storage Classes**: EBS/EFS provisioners\n- **Network Policies**: Pod-level security\n\n#### **Customized Mode**\nBring your own infrastructure:\n- Use existing ingress controllers\n- Custom authentication systems\n- External identity providers\n- Integrate with existing RBAC\n\n### **Security Features**\n\n1. **Secure by Default**:\n   - Templates enforce image allowlists (no arbitrary images)\n   - Resource bounds prevent resource exhaustion\n   - Owner-only access mode for private workspaces\n\n2. **Multi-Tenant Isolation**:\n   - Namespace-based separation\n   - Network policies restrict pod communication\n   - RBAC controls workspace CRUD operations\n\n3. **Authentication & Authorization**:\n   - OIDC integration (GitHub, LDAP, SAML via Dex)\n   - Kubernetes RBAC for workspace access\n   - JWT tokens for API access\n   - Pod exec restrictions (owner-only)\n\n4. **AWS Integration**:\n   - KMS for JWT signing\n   - SSM for secure remote connections (no SSH ingress)\n   - EBS/EFS for persistent storage\n   - IAM roles via service accounts (IRSA)\n\n### **Connection Methods**\n\n1. **Web Browser** (JupyterLab UI):\n   - HTTPS ingress via Traefik\n   - OIDC authentication flow\n   - Session cookies for persistence\n\n2. **Remote IDE** (VS Code):\n   - Tunneling via SSM (no direct SSH)\n   - JWT bearer tokens for authentication\n   - WebSocket connections (planned)\n\n3. **CLI/API**:\n   - Extension API for programmatic access\n   - Bearer token authentication\n   - Connection URL generation\n\n### **Operational Features**\n\n- **Idle Shutdown**: Automatic workspace termination after inactivity\n- **Resource Scheduling**: GPU support, node affinity, tolerations\n- **Storage Management**: Dynamic PVC provisioning, secondary volumes\n- **Lifecycle Hooks**: PreStop/PostStart container hooks\n- **Health Monitoring**: 